{
  "program": "G",
  "title": "Training bigram gating leaves most wheel grammar exceptions",
  "hard": false,
  "on_path": false,
  "statement": "A character-bigram gate applied to the same fragment wheels reduces median Stolfi out-of-grammar mass only from .380 to .347 in ZL and .379 to .351 in IT, compared with observed .051 and .047. Median token-length total variation changes from .0508 to .0447 and .0382 to .0374; matched one-edit rates remain .0243 and .0255 versus .0409 and .0427 for retained real pairs. The gate needs approximately 1.07 candidate draws per emitted token. These are public practice results and ten-seed ranges describe only generator variation.",
  "check": "Try other prespecified, compact structural constraints fitted exclusively to independent training material; measure model description length and exception support as well as length and neighborhood fit. Use independent text witnesses, folio-level uncertainty and a reviewed held-out scorer before broad claims.",
  "method": "Retain P-G-033 length-weighted wheel banks and 10% previous-fragment sharing. Construct the set of all adjacent raw EVA character pairs, including ^ and $ word-boundary markers, occurring in certain ASCII-lowercase paragraph words on ZL public training pages; this set contains 312 pairs. For a complete candidate after optional sharing, accept always if every boundary-augmented character bigram appears in that set; otherwise accept with probability .1 and redraw on rejection. This gate uses only training data and does not consult the Stolfi grammar, which is used afterward as an evaluation measure. Compare gate to no gate using seeds 51001\u201351010 for public ZL and IT evaluation lengths. Sequence boundaries reset sharing.",
  "metrics": "Use P-G-033 metrics and length-stratum matching: token/type EVA-basic length TV, grammar-exception fraction, exact repeat and one-edit rates, attempts per token, and real and synthetic length-matched comparison. Sampling ranges quantify only Monte Carlo variation. A 312-pair whitelist is a model component; we do not claim a measured description-length advantage over the full grammar.",
  "reproduction": "Extract the registry item P-G-024 as /tmp/p-g-024.json; download https://www.ic.unicamp.br/~stolfi/EXPORT/voynich/00-06-07-word-grammar/txt.n.html to /tmp/stolfi-grammar.html; run the embedded Python from the repository root with PYTHONPATH=. and pinned corpus data.",
  "input_sha256": {
    "registry_item": "df21ed0d0b628ee0a12e60b38a007830b8ce51c632b3643e14e45729d5f46400",
    "grammar_html": "a74a5224544d50f131f5b133023c835ad971dfef4098d4aa883026c7fb42bd55",
    "script": "f442d6a38421bf2dc229657a47aaa2baf0ca86266d5033aca9a8860bd1157c4c"
  },
  "limitations": "The whitelist is manuscript-derived, and ZL and IT are two transcriptions of much of the same manuscript rather than independent works. Retaining the same length weights and grammar evaluator makes this a limited ablation, not an exhaustive search for compact rules. Per-seed ranges are not folio confidence intervals.",
